diag-router (linux-msm/diag 23c12c1) changes for the Duo's modem DIAG over QRTR. Build static for aarch64 with
libqrtr: make HAVE_LIBUDEV=0 HAVE_LIBQRTR=1 CFLAGS="-O2 -DHAS_LIBQRTR=1" LDFLAGS="-static -lqrtr" diag-router
- peripheral.c: "set all F3 masks" (0x7d 0x05) passed a NULL range and crashed the router.
- watch.c: a client write that got EAGAIN (unix SEQPACKET peer queue full, e.g. the modem's boot burst) stayed
  pending forever; the client queue stalled and, through flow control, the router stopped reading the modem's
  data channel. Requeue the message and retry once the socket is writable.
- peripheral-qrtr.c: forward every non-HDLC frame of a QRTR packet (the modem packs several), 64 KiB receive
  buffer, per-peripheral data counters every 10 s.
- diag_cntl.c: feature mask as the downstream APPS diag (MASK_CENTRALIZATION, no MASTER_SETS_COMMON_MASK); with
  DIAG ID support send masks, DIAGMODE and tx mode after the DIAG ID exchange, as downstream does; log range reports.
- diag.c: line-buffered stdout for log files.

